meta {
  name: Book Session
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/student/counselling/sessions
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
  Authorization: Bearer {{studentAccessToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "availability_id": "{{availabilityId}}",
    "session_mode": "video_call",
    "session_type": "career",
    "booking_reason": "Need guidance for higher studies"
  }
}

script:pre-request {
  const token = bru.getEnvVar("studentAccessToken") || bru.getEnvVar("accessToken");
  const availabilityId = bru.getEnvVar("availabilityId");
  if (!token) {
    throw new Error("studentAccessToken is not set. Run Student Verify OTP/Login first.");
  }
  bru.setEnvVar("studentAccessToken", token);
  if (!availabilityId) {
    throw new Error("availabilityId is not set. Run List Available Slots first and pick a slot id from time_slots array.");
  }
}

script:post-response {
  if (res.status === 201) {
    const data = res.getBody();
    if (data.data && data.data.id) {
      bru.setEnvVar("sessionId", data.data.id);
    }
  }
}

docs {
  Books a counselling session for the logged-in student.
  Requires: student access token.

  ## Fields
  - availability_id : required, slot id from time_slots[].id in List Available Slots response
  - session_mode    : required, "voice_call" | "video_call"
  - session_type    : required, "career" | "academic" | "personal" | "mental_health"
  - booking_reason  : optional, max 500 chars

  ## Booking cutoff
  A slot can only be booked at least 10 minutes before its scheduled
  start time. E.g. for a 4:00 PM slot, booking is allowed up to and
  including 3:50 PM; attempting at 3:55 PM returns 400 "Sessions can
  only be booked at least 10 minutes before the scheduled start time".
  If the slot's start time has already passed entirely (e.g. booking a
  4:00 PM slot at 4:30 PM), it returns 400 "This slot's scheduled time
  has already passed" instead.

  ## MindCare-only restrictions
  These apply only when the slot's counsellor has counsellor_type
  "mindcare" — Academic counselling has neither restriction.
  - The student must be an enrolled BeaconU student (has an active
    Enrollment at any college). Otherwise 403 "Only enrolled students can
    book MindCare sessions".
  - Lifetime cap of 3 completed MindCare sessions per student. Cancelled
    sessions don't count against the cap. Once reached, 409 "You've used
    all 3 of your MindCare sessions".

  ## Fee logic (no need to pass session_fee)
  Fee is taken automatically from the slot's session_fee.
  Falls back to counsellor's default fee if slot has no fee set.

  ## Payment (Razorpay)
  If the resolved fee > 0, run Create Payment Order first and complete
  Razorpay Checkout. Payment confirmation is received via the Razorpay
  `payment.captured` webhook (POST /api/v1/webhooks/counselling/razorpay),
  which marks the order as paid server-side. This endpoint then verifies
  that marker for (availability_id, student) — no payment fields are
  passed in the request body.

  If the slot is free (fee = 0), this endpoint can be called directly
  after Create Payment Order returns payment_required: false.

  ## Wallet
  On successful booking, session_fee is credited directly to the counsellor's wallet.

  ## Google Meet (all sessions)
  If Google Meet is configured on the server, a Google Calendar event with
  an auto-generated Meet link is created for this session at booking time
  (regardless of session_mode — "voice_call" or "video_call"), with the
  counsellor and student added as attendees (calendar invite emails sent
  to both). The response's data.meeting_url / data.meeting_id reflect this
  new event.

  If Meet is not configured or the Calendar API call fails, booking still
  succeeds with meeting_url/meeting_id as null — the counsellor can set
  them manually via PATCH /api/v1/counsellor/sessions/:id/meeting.
}
